imed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced 2026-11-23 PST on gerrit main 053604a2618 with real exception chains (ModelAPIError <- anthropic.APIConnectionError <- httpx.ProxyError 403 <- httpcore.ProxyError), alone and as 2 legs of a FallbackExceptionGroup: both RETRY_NOW, retryable, 'Transient connection blip', diagnostic without any proxy mention. Implemented in local commit 25c97fe795f (worktree bug-f8d9-proxy-refusal): both now CHANGE_SETTINGS, non-retryable, error_type proxy_refused, proxy text in the diagnostic message, and message_for returns the proxy-refusal message. Beyond the plan: close_gate_remedy also returns the proxy message for that outcome; without it the close gate would tell the operator to install the agents extra and set an API key, because it maps every CHANGE_SETTINGS to UNAVAILABLE_REMEDY. Red check: 7 of the 13 new tests fail on the pre-fix code; the 6 that pass there are the unchanged-behaviour guards (ConnectError/ConnectTimeout, plain ModelAPIError, proxy 5xx, retryable leg wins, cause cycle). _map complexity 14 -> 13; lint, typecheck and ratchets exit 0; make verify running.","timestamp":1795429223311135001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review 1 BLOCKED on 3 real gaps, all verified against the code: (a) _llm_error_exit_code printed its message only for retryable outcomes, so a now-non-retryable refusal surfaced nothing on the raised-error path; (b) close_gate_remedy maps any CHANGE_SETTINGS to the install-the-extra remedy (already handled in the first commit, now also tested end to end through _raise_close_failure, with a distinct PROXY_REFUSED_REMEDY so the close error does not repeat the hint); (c) model_classes.should_fall_back would stop the fallback chain at a proxy-refused primary; it now still advances, since a refusal is per host. Also: the group diagnostic carries the legs' distinct proxy texts, and docs/config.md names the refusal under CHANGE_SETTINGS. Plan updated; review 2 PASS (signed). Amended as 2a99872bfc4 (same Change-Id); 17 new tests and 402 existing tests on the changed paths pass. make verify run 1 discarded: the worktree changed under it. Rerun started 03:22 PST.","timestamp":1795432930428619001}],"created_at":1795413052009540001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"40d3c2eb-1876-4347-98a1-ac9b698d79c0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7279-b619-cb42-40b8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nWhen an egress proxy refuses a gate LLM request by policy, the failure classifier labels it \"Transient connection blip — retry immediately\" (RETRY_NOW, exit 11). Retrying cannot succeed: the refusal is a fixed proxy policy, not a blip.\n\nObserved 2026-11-22 21:44 PST: `review-plan antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow` run inside the Claude Code Bash sandbox without `api.anthropic.com` in the command's allowed hosts returned INDETERMINATE with `llm-degrade: RETRY_NOW — Transient connection blip`. The FallbackModel sub-exceptions, captured by wrapping `run_failure.interpret_failure` around a single-turn `get_runner(resolve_gate_config(\".\")).run(...)` call, were for both candidates: `ModelAPIError(Connection error.) <- anthropic.APIConnectionError <- httpx.ProxyError(\"403 not in this command's allowed_domains ...\") <- httpcore.ProxyError`. The same probe with `api.anthropic.com` allowed returned a completion. So the LLM transport does route through the proxy (the c8118c62e81 fix works); only the classification is wrong.\n\nCause in code: `src/rebar/llm/failure.py::_map` has no arm for `httpx.ProxyError`; the wrapped `ModelAPIError` without a status code falls to the final `ModelAPIError -> RETRY_NOW` arm, and the fallback-group classifier lets any retryable leg win.\n\n## Approach\nReproduced 2026-11-23 PST on gerrit main 053604a2618: `ModelAPIError` <- `anthropic.APIConnectionError` <- `httpx.ProxyError(\"403 not in this command's allowed_domains\")`, alone and as both legs of a `FallbackExceptionGroup`, classifies `RETRY_NOW`, retryable (exit 11), \"Transient connection blip\", diagnostic with no proxy mention.\n\nRoot cause: `httpx.ProxyError` is a `TransportError`, not a `ConnectError`, so no httpx arm of `failure.py::_map` matches. The status-less `ModelAPIError` hits the final `ModelAPIError -> RETRY_NOW` arm, and `_classify_fallback_group` lets a retryable leg win. httpcore raises `ProxyError(\"<status> <reason>\")` for a non-2xx CONNECT; a 4xx is proxy policy (allowlist refusal, 407), so a retry cannot help.\n\nFix:\n1. `failure._proxy_refusal(exc)`: walks `exc` and its `__cause__`/`__context__` chain (bounded, cycle-safe). It returns the proxy text for an `httpx.ProxyError` starting with a 4xx status, else `None`. A proxy 5xx and `ConnectError`/`ConnectTimeout` are not refusals.\n2. `_map`'s tail (`ModelAPIError -> RETRY_NOW`, the `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` default) moves to `_map_tail`, which returns `CHANGE_SETTINGS` (non-retryable) first for a refusal. `_map` complexity drops from 14 to 13.\n3. `_classify_fallback_group`: a retryable leg still wins. Otherwise a group whose every leg is a refusal is `CHANGE_SETTINGS`, not `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`.\n4. `_base_diagnostic` sets the allowlisted `error_type: proxy_refused` and appends the proxy text (redactor applies) to `message`; for a group it appends the legs' distinct texts in leg order, joined by \"; \".\n5. `PROXY_REFUSED_MESSAGE` (parallel to `CONTENT_FILTER_MESSAGE`) names the proxy refusal as a fixed policy, not a transient blip, and gives the remedy (allow the provider host through the proxy). `message_for(..., error_type=None)` returns it for `CHANGE_SETTINGS` with `error_type == \"proxy_refused\"`. The 3 callers (`_cli/_llm_commands.py` x2, `_commands/completion_verifier_run.py`) pass `diagnostic.get(\"error_type\")`. The keyword is optional, and no config key, env var or flag is added.\n6. `_llm_commands._llm_error_exit_code` (raised-LLMError path) prints `llm-degrade: <class> — <message>` for every classified outcome, not only a retryable one. The exit code is unchanged: 11 when retryable, else 1.\n7. `close_gate_remedy` maps any `CHANGE_SETTINGS` to `UNAVAILABLE_REMEDY` (\"install the agents extra and set a model API key\"). For `error_type == \"proxy_refused\"` it returns a new `PROXY_REFUSED_REMEDY` instead (not an install or key problem; allow the host through the proxy, then close again), checked first.\n8. `model_classes.should_fall_back` (FallbackModel `fallback_on`) advances only on retryable or `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` primaries. A refusal is per host, so it also returns True when `_proxy_refusal(exc)` finds one: a later leg on another host may be allowed. Credential, input and quota primaries still surface.\n9. `docs/config.md`: the `CHANGE_SETTINGS` table row also names the proxy 4xx refusal.\n\nAC reading: \"cause chain holds an httpx.ProxyError\" covers a single failure and a group whose every leg is a refusal. A group that also has a retryable leg keeps retryable precedence (that leg may succeed); one that also has a non-proxy hard failure keeps `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/failure.py`, `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/completion_verifier_run.py`, `docs/config.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_proxy_refusal.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\nNew `tests/unit/test_llm_proxy_refusal.py` with real chains (`ModelAPIError` <- `APIConnectionError` <- `httpx.ProxyError` <- `httpcore.ProxyError`):\n- 2-leg all-refused group (the AC test) and single leg: `CHANGE_SETTINGS`, not retryable, `error_type` `proxy_refused`, proxy text in `message`, `message_for` gives `PROXY_REFUSED_MESSAGE`. Also 407, and a raw `httpx.ProxyError` 403.\n- Surfacing: `_llm_error_exit_code` on a raised `LLMUnavailableError` carrying that outcome returns 1 and prints the proxy message, never \"Transient connection blip\". `_disposition_exit_code` on a degraded verdict prints it and does not return 11. `_raise_close_failure` raises with `PROXY_REFUSED_MESSAGE` and `PROXY_REFUSED_REMEDY`, without `UNAVAILABLE_REMEDY`, returncode 1.\n- Fallback: `should_fall_back` is True for a refused primary and False for a 401. A group with 2 identical 403 texts and a 407 carries each text once.\n- Edges: refused + 429 group stays `WAIT_AND_RETRY`; refused + 401 group stays `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`; a proxy 502 keeps `RETRY_NOW`; a cause cycle terminates. `ConnectError`/`ConnectTimeout` (alone and wrapped) and a plain `ModelAPIError` keep `RETRY_NOW`.\n- Red check: the behaviour-change tests fail on pre-fix code. The unchanged-behaviour guards pass on both by design. Existing tests on the changed paths keep passing, and `make verify` passes before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A gate LLM failure whose cause chain holds an `httpx.ProxyError` from a proxy refusal (CONNECT answered with a 4xx) is not classified RETRY_NOW or WAIT_AND_RETRY, and its surfaced message names the proxy refusal.\n- [ ] A unit test builds that cause chain (ModelAPIError <- APIConnectionError <- httpx.ProxyError 403) inside a FallbackExceptionGroup and asserts the non-retryable class; existing ConnectError/ConnectTimeout cases keep RETRY_NOW.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/failure.py","reason":"classify a 4xx proxy refusal CHANGE_SETTINGS; diagnostic, message and close-gate remedy"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"should_fall_back keeps the chain going past a proxy-refused primary"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"pass error_type to message_for; print llm-degrade for non-retryable raised outcomes"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_verifier_run.py","reason":"pass error_type to message_for"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"CHANGE_SETTINGS row names the proxy refusal"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_proxy_refusal.py","reason":"new classifier and surfacing tests for proxy refusal chains"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e911a66c-6de2-4491-9e34-5c7c972f90f2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f8d9-1d45-f3f4-4ab7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Proxy policy refusal of a gate LLM call is classified as a transient blip","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["de1bd006-3a26-4c2c-a8d8-ae33b25bd331","40d3c2eb-1876-4347-98a1-ac9b698d79c0","e911a66c-6de2-4491-9e34-5c7c972f90f2","0a7de3ae-f345-437f-a4d6-e582dc6aa88a","a08e19e0-8bc8-442b-b191-919d364914e3","4100130a-1efe-4007-a64b-258fb13dc5f7","db5684fc-ab39-48a1-b396-9c7f279c907c","b9e7acd5-260c-4087-8bac-eaf401b9879e","d8ff0c27-4646-4302-9a0d-f8475c882dab","510a72c8-834d-41f5-9e23-1f7752b4c770","7bf23997-c35f-4771-99f1-29887b14f773","43ae605c-9272-426b-81e4-6d08f1525519"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795432930428619002,"uuid":"9957da41-a13d-49a8-b3fc-91f4da218fce"}